# SDT UI/UX skill

Read the project's UI/UX instruction files before doing UI work; this skill routes
to them and never restates them.

1. Read `context/instructions/ui.md` **before any UI change** (the doctrine).
2. Read `context/instructions/ui-tokens.md` when choosing or changing colour,
   spacing, type or radius tokens — before touching a literal value.
3. Read `context/instructions/ui-components.md` when building or changing a
   component; `context/instructions/ui-layout.md` when arranging a surface.
4. Read `context/instructions/ui-accessibility.md` for any interactive or visual
   change, plus the accessibility review.
5. Read `context/instructions/ui-motion.md` when animating; `ui-taste.md` for
   layout, visual direction and copy review; `ui-performance.md` for budgets;
   `ui-adapters.md` when mapping the framework's idioms.

Verify a rendered result with `context/instructions/browser.md` before claiming a
layout looks right. If a number in an instruction conflicts with the installed
tool, re-verify the tool and follow the project.
